\v 79 to¦38589 shine¦38589 on those in darkness¦38593 and¦38594 sitting¦38597 in the¦38595 shadow¦38595 of¦38596 death¦38596;\x + \xo 1:79: \xt Isa 9:2.\x*
\q1 to guide us¦38602 onto the road of peace¦38605.”
\p
\v 80 The¦38606 young boy grew and his spirit¦38612 was¦38611 also strengthened¦38611, and he lived in¦38615 the wilderness¦38617 until¦38618 he started his ministry to \add the people of\add* Yisrael¦38624.
\c 2
\s1 Yeshua's birth in Bethlehem
\rem /s1 The Birth of Jesus
\r (Mat. 1:18-25)
\p
\v 1 At that time¦38629, Caesar¦38634 Augustus¦38635 sent a decree¦38632 that everyone throughout the empire needed to¦38637 register¦38637 \add in a census\add*.
\v 2 (This census was conducted when¦38650 Quirinius was the¦38651 governor¦38650 of Syria¦38652.)
\v 3 Everyone had to \add officially\add* register¦38658 in the¦38661 city¦38667 where they were \add born\add*.
\p
\v 4 Because¦38690 Yosef was a descendant of \add King\add* David, he left the town of \nd Nazareth¦38677\nd* in the Galilee¦38674 \add region\add* and¦38669 went¦38668 down to David's town of Bethlehem¦38689 in Yudea¦38681
\v 5 to¦38699 register¦38699 along with¦38701 Maria¦38702, his pregnant¦38710 fiancée.
\v 6 While they were¦38729 in Bethlehem, the time¦38725 came for her¦38735 to¦38734 give birth
\v 7 and so Maria bore¦38737 her¦38740 first¦38742 son¦38739 and wrapped him in strips of cloth and slept him in an \add empty\add* feeding trough, because¦38753 they had missed out on the¦38759 guest¦38760 room¦38760.
\s1 The shepherds and the messengers
