\p
\v 8 In that same¦38770 area, there were some shepherds¦38762 staying out in the fields¦38772 where they kept¦38774 watch¦38776 over¦38779 their¦38782 flocks¦38781 at night¦38778.
\v 9 A messenger¦38785 sent by \nd Yahweh\nd* approached¦38787 them, and \nd Yahweh's\nd* radiance shone around¦38793 them, and they¦38798 were¦38798 very frightened.
\v 10 “Don't¦38807 be¦38816 scared,” the¦38805 messenger¦38806 told them¦38804, “because¦38810 I'm bringing you¦38812 a good¦38811 message¦38811 that¦38815 will¦38816 bring great¦38814 happiness to¦38819 all¦38819 people¦38821
\v 11 because¦38822 a saviour¦38826 for all people was born¦38823 today¦38825 in¦38832 David's town¦38833. He's the¦38833 \nd messiah¦38829\nd*, \nd Yahweh¦38830\nd*,
\v 12 and this¦38836 is¦38836 how you'll know him: you'll find¦38842 a baby¦38843 wrapped in strips of cloth and sleeping in a feeding trough.”
\p
\v 13 Then¦38851 suddenly¦38852 lots of¦38858 heavenly¦38859 soldiers joined the messenger¦38856, praising¦38861 \nd God¦38864\nd* and¦38865 saying¦38866,
\v 14 “Let all honour be given to \nd God¦38870\nd* in¦38868 the¦38869 highest¦38869, and¦38871 peace¦38874 on¦38872 earth¦38873 to all people¦38877 along with¦38879 good¦38879 will.”
\p
\v 15 Then¦38880 as¦38882 the messengers¦38892 left them¦38887 and¦38907 went¦38883 \add up\add* into the sky, the shepherds¦38897 said¦38898 to¦38900 each other, “Well, we'll certainly go into Bethlehem¦38906 so we can see¦38908 what this¦38911 was about that¦38914 \nd Yahweh¦38916\nd* has¦38913 let us¦38918 know¦38917 about.”
\p
\v 16 So¦38919 they hurried¦38921 \add into town\add* and asked around to find Maria¦38928 and Yosef¦38931, and \add also\add* the baby¦38934 sleeping in¦38936 the feeding trough.
\v 17 \add ≈When¦38940 they met them\add*, they explained what they'd been told about the¦38950 young baby.
\v 18 Everyone who heard¦38956 this was amazed at what the shepherds¦38965 told them¦38967,
\v 19 but¦38969 Maria¦38970 treasured¦38972 all¦38971 of these¦38976 messages¦38975 in her¦38982 heart¦38980 and \add often\add* thought about them.
\v 20 Finally the¦38986 shepherds¦38987 returned¦38985 \add back to their fields\add*—they were worshipping and praising¦38990 \nd God¦38992\nd* for¦38993 what they'd heard¦38996 and how they'd seen¦38998 it exactly like they'd been told.
\s1 The child is named Yeshua
