\p
\v 21 When¦39003 the baby was eight¦39010 days¦39008 old and¦39003 hence the time¦39030 for his¦39021 circumcision¦39012, he was given the name¦39020 \nd Yeshua\nd* as instructed by \add God's\add* messenger¦39028 even before¦39029 he was conceived¦39031 in¦39034 the womb.\x + \xo 2:21: a \xt Lev 12:3; \xo b \xt Luk 1:31.\x*
\s1 Yeshua is dedicated in the temple
\rem /s1 Jesus Is Presented in the Temple
\p
\v 22 Then¦39038 when¦39039 the time¦39042 of the \add mother's\add* purification¦39044 was fulfilled¦39040 as per Mosheh's¦39051 instructions, they¦39052 took him¦39053 down to Yerushalem¦39055 to be dedicated to \nd Yahweh¦39059\nd*
\v 23 to follow what is written¦39061 in Yahweh's law¦39064: Every¦39067 firstborn male¦39068 is set aside for Yahweh\x + \xo 2:23: \xt Exo 13:2,12.\x*
\v 24 and¦39076 hence a sacrifice¦39079 has¦39082 to be made, which¦39077 according¦39080 to that¦39077 law¦39085 is a pair of turtledoves¦39088 or¦39089 a pair of young¦39091 doves¦39092.\x + \xo 2:22-24: \xt Lev 12:6-8.\x*
\rem /s1 The Prophecy of Simeon
\p
\v 25 Now listen, there was a man named Simeon¦39103 in¦39098 Yerushalem¦39099 and he was godly¦39111 and committed, waiting¦39112 for¦39112 God to rescue Yisrael¦39115. He was \add full\add* of¦39115 the¦39114 holy¦39120 \nd spirit¦39117\nd*
\v 26 and¦39123 the \nd spirit¦39132\nd* had¦39126 told him¦39125 that he¦39142 wouldn't die without seeing Yahweh's \nd messiah¦39144\nd*.
\v 27 He¦39147 had¦39170 come¦39147 to the temple¦39153 listening to the \nd spirit¦39150\nd* at¦39155 just the same time¦39156 as the parents brought¦39157 in the baby \nd Yeshua¦39163\nd* in order to follow the rituals for¦39173 new parents.
\v 28 Simeon took the baby into his arms¦39182 and blessed¦39185 \nd God¦39187\nd* and said¦39189,
\v 29 “Now, Yahweh¦39195, you can send¦39191 your¦39194 slave¦39193 away¦39191 in¦39200 peace¦39201 as you promised
\v 30 because¦39202 I've set my¦39206 eyes¦39205 on your¦39209 salvation¦39208
\v 31 which¦39210 you¦39211 have prepared¦39211 in¦39212 front¦39213 of¦39214 everyone:
\v 32 a light¦39217 so the non-Jews can understand, and the greatest gift from and for your¦39224 people¦39223 of¦39224 Yisrael¦39225.”\x + \xo 2:32: \xt Isa 42:6; 49:6; 52:10.\x*
\p
\v 33 The baby's parents were amazed¦39236 at¦39237 the¦39238 things being¦39239 spoken¦39239 about him¦39241,
\v 34 and Simeon¦39245 blessed¦39243 them¦39244 and said¦39247 to Maria¦39249, “Listen¦39253, this¦39254 boy has been chosen to cause both the rise and the fall¦39257 of¦39261 many people in¦39262 Yisrael¦39264, and \add sent as\add* a sign¦39267 but¦39242 one which many people will oppose.
\v 35 Also¦39269 even as you¦39270 experience incredible grief in the future, it will allow the thoughts of many¦39282 hearts¦39283 to be¦39279 revealed¦39279.”
\rem /s1 The Prophecy of Anna
\p
\v 36 Also¦39286 there, was a prophetess¦39289 named Hanna¦39288 (the daughter¦39290 of Fanuel from¦39309 the tribe¦39293 of Asher). She was very elderly, having been married for seven¦39308 years¦39307
