\v 22 \wj but¦49356 when¦49336 someone stronger¦49339 than¦49339 him arrives and overpowers him, he'll even take¦49351 the body armour that¦49353 the \+add landowner\+add* put his trust¦49354 in¦49352, and then relieve him of all his goods.\wj*
\p
\v 23 “\wj Anyone who doesn't \+add follow\+add* me is¦49370 against¦49368 me, and¦49371 anyone who doesn't gather¦49374 with¦49375 us, \+add wants to\+add* scatter¦49377 us.\wj*\x + \xo 11:23: \xt Mrk 9:40.\x*
