\p
\v 14 “\wj Man,\wj*” Yeshua responded¦50472, “\wj who¦50475 said¦50472 that I'm the judge¦50478 or¦50480 arbitrator¦50481 over¦50482 you¦50483 all¦50483?\wj*”
\v 15 Then¦50486 he¦50485 told them¦50488, “\wj Keep alert to avoid all¦50493 greediness¦50495, because¦50496 a person's life¦50504 is¦50508 not¦50497 about gaining lots of¦50509 possessions¦50511.\wj*”
\p
\v 16 Then¦50516 he¦50515 told them¦50519 all this parable¦50517, “\wj One time a rich¦50524 man's¦50522 farm produced a really good harvest.\wj*
\v 17 \wj So¦50528 he¦50529 started figuring out what to do, ‘What should I do? I don't¦50537 have¦50538 anywhere to store my¦50544 harvest.’\wj*
\v 18 \wj ‘Ah,’ he¦50546 said¦50546, ‘I know what I'll do¦50548. I'll knock down¦50549 my barns¦50552 and build¦50558 bigger ones, and then¦50545 I'll store all¦50563 my grain¦50566 and other produce in there¦50562.\wj*
\v 19 \wj Then¦50573 I'll¦50574 be able to tell¦50574 my¦50577 soul¦50576: Soul¦50579, you've got enough good¦50582 things now to be able to relax for¦50584 many¦50586 years¦50585 of resting¦50587, eating¦50588, drinking¦50589, and¦50573 being¦50590 happy.’\wj*
\v 20 \wj But¦50611 \+nd God¦50596\+nd* said¦50591 to him¦50593, ‘How foolish! Tonight I'll be demanding your¦50607 soul¦50603 and¦50611 then who will everything you stored up go to?’\wj*
