\p
\v 22 Then¦50628 Yeshua told his followers¦50631, “\wj That's why I'm telling you¦50637 all¦50637 not to worry¦50639 about your¦50640 lifestyle: what to eat¦50644 or what to wear,\wj*
\v 23 \wj because¦50652 your life¦50653 is more than food¦50657 and¦50658 your body¦50660 is more than clothing¦50662.\wj*
\v 24 \wj Look at the¦50669 ravens¦50670. They don't¦50673 plant seeds or harvest crops and they have no storerooms¦50682 or barns, yet \+nd God¦50689\+nd* keeps them fed¦50690, and \+add humans\+add* are worth a lot more than¦50697 birds¦50699.\wj*
\v 25 \wj Which¦50700 of¦50702 you¦50703 can add¦50711 even an¦50712 hour¦50712 to¦50707 your¦50702 life by spending more time worrying¦50704?\wj*
\v 26 \wj So¦50715 if¦50714 you¦50721 can't¦50716 even¦50716 do something small like that, why¦50723 worry¦50728 about¦50724 bigger things?\wj*
\v 27 \wj Look at how the lilies¦50731 grow. They don't¦50745 go to¦50743 work or make \+add fabric\+add*, yet even¦50745 \+add King\+add* Solomon¦50746 at the height of his¦50751 fame wasn't dressed as well as one¦50754 of them.\wj*\x + \xo 12:27: \xt 1Ki 10:4-7; 2Ch 9:3-6.\x*
\v 28 \wj So if¦50757 \+nd God¦50781\+nd* dresses¦50783 the weeds in¦50760 the paddock that are here¦50773 today¦50774 and¦50775 incinerated tomorrow¦50776, how¦50784 much¦50784 more would he look after you¦50787 all¦50787—you with little¦50788 faith¦50788?\wj*
\p
