\v 18 \wj I'm going¦53432 to leave and go \+add back\+add* to my¦53436 father¦53435 to tell¦53438 him¦53439, “Father¦53440, I've disobeyed \+add God\+add* and \+add ≡dishonoured\+add* you¦53447\wj*
\v 19 \wj and I'm no¦53449 longer¦53449 worthy¦53451 to¦53452 be¦53452 called¦53452 your son¦53453. Take me¦53457 on as¦53459 one¦53460 of your workers.” ’\wj*
\p
\v 20 “\wj So¦53464 he¦53466 got¦53465 up¦53465 and headed back to¦53467 his father, but¦53473 his father saw¦53477 him coming¦53466 from a distance and felt¦53483 sorry for him. He ran¦53485 and hugged \+add his son\+add* and kissed¦53494 him,\wj*
\v 21 \wj and the¦53500 son said¦53496, ‘Father¦53504, I've disobeyed \+add God\+add* and \+add ≡dishonoured\+add* you¦53511 and I'm no¦53513 longer¦53513 worthy¦53515 to¦53516 be¦53516 called¦53516 your¦53518 son.’\wj*
\v 22 \wj But¦53545 the father¦53530 ordered his slaves¦53533, ‘Quickly¦53537, bring¦53539 out¦53539 the best robe¦53542 and dress¦53546 him¦53547 in¦53546 it, and put a ring¦53551 on his hand¦53554 and sandals¦53557 on his feet¦53560.\wj*
\v 23 \wj Then get the grain-fed¦53569 calf¦53567 and¦53573 slaughter it¦53572 so we¦53577 can celebrate with a feast,\wj*
