\v 28 \wj But¦53672 the \+add older\+add* son was¦53664 angry and didn't¦53667 want¦53668 to go in¦53670, however his¦53675 father¦53674 came out¦53676 and implored¦53677 him¦53679 \+add to join them\+add*.\wj*
\v 29 \wj ‘Listen¦53687,’ said¦53683 \+add the older son\+add* to his¦53686 father¦53685, ‘I've worked for you for however many years¦53689 and¦53681 I've never disobeyed you, yet you never gave¦53702 me¦53700 even a young¦53704 goat¦53704 so that¦53708 I could¦53714 celebrate with¦53709 my¦53712 friends¦53711!\wj*
\v 30 \wj Yet when¦53715 \+em this\+em* son¦53719 of yours comes¦53735 home after using up your¦53721 money living¦53730 with¦53731 prostitutes¦53733, then you¦53737 slaughter the¦53741 fattened calf¦53743 for¦53738 him¦53738!’\wj*
\v 31 \wj ‘Son,’ answered the¦53756 father, ‘you¦53749 have always¦53750 been here with¦53751 me¦53752, and¦53754 everything I have is yours¦53758.\wj*
\v 32 \wj But¦53773 it's¦53765 right to be happy and excited, because¦53766 your¦53769 brother¦53768 was dead¦53771 and now he's alive \+add again\+add*—he was lost¦53777 and now he's found¦53780.’\wj* ”
\c 16
